      "extract": "In 1867 Lord Kelvin [1] proposed that atoms, which at the time were considered as elementary particles, are knotted vortex tubes in ether. For about 20 years his theory was taken seriously, and motivated an extensive study of knots. The results obtained at the time by Tait [2] remain a classic contribution to mathematical knot theory [3]. More recently the idea that elementary particles can be identiﬁed with",
      "extractCut": true,
      "blocks": [
        "library/arxiv-hep-th-9610193v1/blocks/prose-page-002"
      ]
    },
